{title: Arise and Build!}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]1. [E]The [Em]Lord [Am]has [C]laid the firm foundation,
[F]And [C]He has given us the goal
[C]To [Dm]bring the Light to every nation,
[G]To [Em]share [Em7]the Hope with [G]every [Am]soul.

Verse 2
The [C]One who calls is our Provider;
[F]We [C]do not join this task [F]alone,
[Am7]For [Dm]He who brings each new beginning
Will [Em]give [Em7]us strength to see [Em7]it [Am]done.

Verse 3
So reach [A#]out to the hand [F]that is beside [C]you.
Together [A#]let us hold [F]His banner high.
[G]That Christ [F]may be exalted,
[G]His commission [E]be fulfilled,
[Am]Let [A7]us [F]hearken* to the call:
Arise [G]and [C]Build!

Verse 4
[C]2. [F]For [C]Jesus Christ is our Foundation;
[F]In [C]Him alone our plans are [F]laid,
[C]To [Dm]count ourselves among the faithful,
To [Em]have God's holy Word [Am]obeyed.

Verse 5
Now [C]as we join this task together,
[F]We [C]trust in Him to see [Cmaj7]us [Fmaj7]on.
[Am]The [Dm]gates of hell cannot withstand us:
[Em]We shall prevail til [Em]we're [Am]done!

Verse 6
[A#]Note: my kids say [F]"hearken" is too old-fashioned a word.
If [C]you [Am]prefer, [F]try substituting the [Am7]word [F]"answer".
